\name{cellucid_stored_remove}
\alias{cellucid_stored_remove}
\title{Remove what this browser keeps}
\usage{
cellucid_stored_remove(
  viewer,
  connection_speeds = FALSE,
  dataset,
  decoder_choices = FALSE,
  everything = FALSE,
  items,
  my_datasets = FALSE,
  saved_states = FALSE
)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{connection_speeds}{The connection speeds remembered per host. \code{TRUE} or \code{FALSE}. Default \code{FALSE}, the viewer's own.}
\item{dataset}{Every kept item of the dataset with this file name (stored_list). Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{decoder_choices}{The decoder choices measured in this browser. \code{TRUE} or \code{FALSE}. Default \code{FALSE}, the viewer's own.}
\item{everything}{Everything no open tab uses, as Remove all. \code{TRUE} or \code{FALSE}. Default \code{FALSE}, the viewer's own.}
\item{items}{Kept items by id (stored_list). A vector or list of text (at least 1 character) (at least 1 item, each once). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{my_datasets}{My datasets: the list and the handles of its files (my_datasets_forget forgets one). \code{TRUE} or \code{FALSE}. Default \code{FALSE}, the viewer's own.}
\item{saved_states}{Every saved state of this browser (history_saved_delete deletes one). \code{TRUE} or \code{FALSE}. Default \code{FALSE}, the viewer's own.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome: a list of \code{connection_speeds} (Hosts whose connection speed was forgotten), \code{decoder_choices} (Decoder choices forgotten), \code{held} (Kept items that stay, in use by an open tab), \code{my_datasets} (Datasets forgotten from My datasets), \code{removed} (Kept items removed), \code{said} (What the dialog says of it), \code{saved_states} (Saved states deleted).
}
\description{
Remove what the Stored dialog removes: kept items by id, all a dataset's kept items, every saved state, My datasets (the list and the files' handles), the connection speeds, the decoder choices, or everything (Remove all). An item an open tab uses stays until that tab closes. Nothing brings it back; the dataset opens again more slowly the first time.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{stored.remove} (Stored). It acts outside the viewer's state and history (a file the person receives in the browser, a publication, or what the browser keeps for later visits), which Undo does not take back: it makes no step of the history.

When an agent (Claude, ChatGPT) runs it, the viewer asks the person first (deletes-saved); from R it is not asked.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_stored_remove(viewer)
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
